^warning: ignoring
--
The program was rejected (E's implicit destructor, see
cpp_implicit_destructor_of_class_derived_from_repeated_base); then the
delete through C passed a pointer to the C subobject to the deallocation
function.  Now the destructor through C is dispatched through C's copy of
the table of D's second A subobject, and the deallocation gets the
address of the most derived object.
